## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/sequenceblend.html
- Summary (EN): Sequence Blend mixes several image layers with a blend factor, interpolating across the numbered image inputs. The page recommends the Blend COP when only two layers need blending.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Sequence Blend mélange plusieurs couches image à l'aide d'un facteur de fondu réparti sur ses entrées numérotées.

- Inputs meaning: ["blend (optional): per-pixel blend amount, scaled by the Blend parameter", "image#: the layers to blend, one per numbered input"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: the layer type the source image accepts", "Invert: inverts the Blend value", "Blend: blend factor from 0 to 1, mapped across all image inputs"]

- Caveats: ["Use the Blend COP instead when you only need to blend two layers"]

